From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:14:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Check a listed remote file's existence from its listing

When read_blob() or read_text() needs neither the content nor the
metadata of a remote file, DirectFileReader::Scan() checked that the file
exists with FileExists(file.path). The bare path drops the size and
modification time the glob's listing put into the OpenFileInfo, so httpfs
sent one HEAD request per file: selecting only filename from a glob over
500 objects took 500 requests, while selecting last_modified as well took
none, because that branch opens the file from the OpenFileInfo. The check
now calls GetStatsIfExists() with the OpenFileInfo, so httpfs answers from
the listing, and a literal path that does not exist still yields no rows.
Local files are not checked, as before. Opening the file with
FILE_FLAGS_NULL_IF_NOT_EXISTS under CACHE_REMOTE_ONLY, as the metadata
branch does, is not an option: the caching wrapper dereferences the null
handle and fails with an internal error.

Carried here until upstream takes it; upstream issue to be filed by the
maintainer, see duckdb/duckdb-r#2977.

---
 src/duckdb/src/function/table/direct_file_reader.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/function/table/direct_file_reader.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/function/table/direct_file_reader.cpp
index c84fdc485e..564912609f 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/function/table/direct_file_reader.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/function/table/direct_file_reader.cpp
@@ -82,7 +82,8 @@ AsyncResult DirectFileReader::Scan(ClientContext &context, GlobalTableFunctionSt
 	} else {
 		// At least verify that the file exist
 		// The globbing behavior in remote filesystems can lead to files being listed that do not actually exist
-		if (is_remote && !fs.FileExists(file.path)) {
+		// Pass the OpenFileInfo so that metadata from the listing can spare a request
+		if (is_remote && !fs.GetStatsIfExists(file)) {
 			done.store(true, std::memory_order_relaxed);
 			return SourceResultType::FINISHED;
 		}
